# DataMCP — the agent-read boundary

This rule scopes AGENTS.md hard rule **22**. The narrative is
[aqp_docs/data-mcp.md](mdc:aqp_docs/data-mcp.md).

## Why this is a boundary

Pre-DataMCP, agents could `import` ORM models, call
`aqp.data.iceberg_catalog` directly, or query Redis vector indexes
free-form. That was an OWASP MCP-Top-10 anti-pattern (context
injection / over-sharing) and a maintenance burden — every new
dataset needed bespoke tool glue.

DataMCP collapses both problems into one catalog with two transports:

- **In-process bridge** —
  [aqp/agents/tools/data_mcp_bridge.py](mdc:aqp/agents/tools/data_mcp_bridge.py)
  auto-installs every registered `DataMCPTool` into
  [`TOOL_REGISTRY`](mdc:aqp/agents/tools/__init__.py).
  `AgentRuntime` sees them through this bridge.
- **External transports** — the same catalog is exposed via the
  FastAPI router at `/mcp/data` and the `aqp-data-mcp` stdio
  binary. Cursor / Claude Desktop / custom scripts use these.

## Hard rules

1. **Agents MUST NOT read Postgres / Iceberg / Redis directly.**
   Inside any module under [aqp/agents/](mdc:aqp/agents) (and any
   `AgentSpec`-driven body), never:
   - `from aqp.persistence.models...`
   - `from aqp.data.iceberg_catalog...`
   - `from aqp.data.duckdb_provider...`
   - `aqp.rag.HierarchicalRAG` direct (that has its own surface;
     agent-side go through the relevant DataMCPTool / RAG-bridged
     tool)
   The rule applies to anything the runtime invokes — agent tool
   bodies, prompt builders, output parsers, custom callbacks.
2. **New agent reads = new `DataMCPTool` subclass.** Subclass
   [`DataMCPTool`](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/base.py) under
   [aqp/data/mcp/tools/](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/tools), decorate with
   `@register_data_mcp_tool`, and let the bridge auto-install. Don't
   carve a one-off path through `aqp/agents/tools/` for "this
   single agent".
3. **Tools must declare a strict args schema, semantic
   description, and policy check.** The schema enables
   JSON-schema-driven prompt formatting; the description shapes
   model selection of the right tool; the policy check sandboxes
   reads (no free-form `SELECT *`).
4. **Refresh metadata via MCP before assuming a schema.** When the
   agent needs to construct an entity-specific read (e.g. "list
   columns for `aqp_silver_equities_bars`"), it should first call
   the catalog MCP tools (e.g. `data.catalog.lineage`,
   `data.catalog.describe_dataset`) rather than relying on cached /
   static knowledge. The static surface in
   [aqp_docs/data-dictionary.md](mdc:aqp_docs/data-dictionary.md) bit-rots
   between releases — MCP is the live source.
5. **Entity-centric data products go through DataMCP too.**
   Subclass [`BaseDataProduct`](mdc:aqp/data/products/base.py) under
   [aqp/data/products/](mdc:aqp/data/products), then add a matching
   `data.entities.*` MCP tool and a `/data/entities/...` REST route.
   See [aqp_docs/data-products.md](mdc:aqp_docs/data-products.md).
6. **The same catalog backs the FastAPI router and the stdio
   binary.** Do not author tool variants per transport — register
   once, both transports pick it up.

## Adding a DataMCP tool — the checklist

1. Subclass `DataMCPTool` (args schema, description, policy check).
2. Implement the read (this is the only place a `from
   aqp.persistence.models...` import is allowed — inside a
   registered MCP tool, not inside an agent body).
3. Decorate with `@register_data_mcp_tool`.
4. The bridge auto-installs into `TOOL_REGISTRY` on next process
   boot. The FastAPI router and stdio binary pick it up via the
   same registry.
5. Add a smoke test under [tests/data/mcp/](mdc:tests/data/mcp).
6. (Optional) Reference the tool from any `AgentSpec.tools` list
   that needs it.

## What the boundary lets you do

- Cursor / Claude Desktop / external scripts can connect to
  `/mcp/data` and use the same tool catalog.
- Tenancy / policy enforcement happens in one place.
- Agents can be replayed deterministically because every read
  flowed through the policy-checked tool catalog.

## Don't

- Don't `import aqp.persistence.models_*` from any module under
  [aqp/agents/](mdc:aqp/agents).
- Don't attach a new file directly to `aqp/agents/tools/`
  bypassing `DataMCPTool` for "speed". The bridge is the
  speed-of-light path; new tools just need to register.
- Don't query Redis vector indexes directly. Use
  [`HierarchicalRAG`](mdc:aqp/rag/hierarchy.py) (or its
  bridged DataMCP tool).
- Don't add a free-form SQL tool. The policy check exists for a
  reason — agents should consume read views / curated catalog
  reads, not run untrusted SQL.
